<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ntare I of Burundi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Ntare I Rushatsi, Ntare Rushatsi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ntare I Rushatsi is remembered in Burundian tradition as the founder of the kingdom's royal dynasty, usually placed in the late 17th century. Accounts describe him uniting chiefdoms in the hills east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-tanganyika">Lake Tanganyika</a> and establishing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacred-kingship">sacred kingship</a> of the mwami. Historians treat the details as legendary, but he stands at the head of the royal line that ruled Burundi until 1966.</p></div>
